From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:15:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: bettervr_settings.ini is read

On Windows ImGuiOverlay's constructor creates the ImGui context, adds the settings handler and loads the file; the Linux backend has no overlay, so the file was never read. The same three calls, once, with no frame and no IniFilename.
---
 src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp b/src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp
index 0ec1cca..3a837d0 100644
--- a/src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendering/renderer_vulkan.cpp
@@ -649,6 +649,14 @@ RND_Renderer::RND_Renderer(XrSession xrSession): m_session(xrSession) {
         }
     }
 
+    // The settings file: vulkan_imgui.cpp's ImGuiOverlay constructor reads it on Windows, and the Linux
+    // backend has no overlay. A context with the settings handler and no frame: it loads the file and
+    // nothing is drawn, nothing takes input from it, and it is never written (no IniFilename).
+    ImGui::CreateContext();
+    ImGui::GetIO().IniFilename = nullptr;
+    InitSettings();
+    ImGui::LoadIniSettingsFromDisk(BETTERVR_SETTINGS_INI);
+
     m_isInitialized = true;
     Log::print<INFO>("Linux RND_Renderer: Initialized with stereo swapchains + intermediates");
 }
